    {
      "id": "scene-04",
      "title": "The Hadamard Gate (H)",
      "durationSeconds": 30,
      "startFrame": 2251,
      "endFrame": 3150,
      "narration": {
        "speaker": "QUALUTION Narrator",
        "text": "How do we create superposition in a quantum circuit? The most important tool is the Hadamard gate, denoted H. Applying H to the ground state |0\u27e9 produces an equal superposition of |0\u27e9 and |1\u27e9.",
        "tone": "Authoritative, pedagogically clear, engaging",
        "pacingWpm": 130
      },
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "The Hadamard gate (H) is the primary gateway to superposition.",
          "startFrame": 2251,
          "endFrame": 2640
        },
        {
          "text": "Applying H to |0\u27e9 yields: H|0\u27e9 = (|0\u27e9 + |1\u27e9) / \u221a2.",
          "startFrame": 2641,
          "endFrame": 3150
        }
      ],
      "onScreenText": [
        {
          "id": "txt_h_matrix",
          "text": "H = (1/\u221a2) [ [1,  1], [1, -1] ]",
          "role": "formula",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            1.5,
            0.1
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "txt_h_op",
          "text": "H |0\u27e9 = |+\u27e9 = (|0\u27e9 + |1\u27e9)/\u221a2",
          "role": "formula",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            -0.5,
            0.1
          ]
        }
      ],
      "visualElements": [
        {
          "id": "vis_4_bg",
          "type": "background_plate",
          "source": "assets/backgrounds/deep_space_grid.png",
          "layer": "background"
        },
        {
          "id": "vis_4_stage",
          "type": "vector_diagram",
          "source": "procedural_blender_object",
          "layer": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "animationActions": [
        {
          "target": "vis_4_stage",
          "action": "fade_in_and_settle",
          "startFrame": 2251,
          "durationFrames": 30
        }
      ],
      "assetsRequired": [
        "deep_space_grid.png",
        "ibm_quantum_palette.blend"
      ],
      "educationalPurpose": "Introduce the Hadamard gate matrix and its mathematical action on basis states.",
      "transitionOut": "smooth_crossfade"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-05",
      "title": "The Plus and Minus States: |+\u27e9 and |-\u27e9",
      "durationSeconds": 30,
      "startFrame": 3151,
      "endFrame": 4050,
      "narration": {
        "speaker": "QUALUTION Narrator",
        "text": "When H acts on |0\u27e9, it creates the plus state |+\u27e9. But when H acts on |1\u27e9, it introduces a negative sign: the minus state |-\u27e9 = (|0\u27e9 - |1\u27e9)/\u221a2. Both have equal 50/50 measurement probabilities, but different internal phases!",
        "tone": "Authoritative, pedagogically clear, engaging",
        "pacingWpm": 130
      },
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "H|0\u27e9 = |+\u27e9 = (|0\u27e9 + |1\u27e9)/\u221a2.  H|1\u27e9 = |-\u27e9 = (|0\u27e9 - |1\u27e9)/\u221a2.",
          "startFrame": 3151,
          "endFrame": 3600
        },
        {
          "text": "Both have 50% probabilities, but completely opposite internal phases!",
          "startFrame": 3601,
          "endFrame": 4050
        }
      ],
      "onScreenText": [
        {
          "id": "txt_plus",
          "text": "|+\u27e9 = (|0\u27e9 + |1\u27e9) / \u221a2",
          "role": "formula",
          "position": [
            -3.5,
            0.5,
            0.1
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "txt_minus",
          "text": "|-\u27e9 = (|0\u27e9 - |1\u27e9) / \u221a2",
          "role": "formula",
          "position": [
            3.5,
            0.5,
            0.1
          ]
        }
      ],
      "visualElements": [
        {
          "id": "vis_5_bg",
          "type": "background_plate",
          "source": "assets/backgrounds/deep_space_grid.png",
          "layer": "background"
        },
        {
          "id": "vis_5_stage",
